# Saved container images, carried by Git LFS.
#
# `docker save` of the Windows cross-toolchain is ~2.2 GB and is what makes
# this repository buildable without the network: without it, a first build
# downloads MXE's upstream tarballs from 117 distinct hosts, any of which can
# disappear. The archive is already compressed - a sample gzips to 99% of its
# original size - so it is stored as-is and never diffed.
#
# Each revision of the image costs another ~2.2 GB of LFS storage
# permanently, because LFS does not deduplicate between versions. Regenerate
# it when the toolchain genuinely changes, not on every image rebuild.
07_Delivery/toolchain/*.tar filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Built deliverables, carried by Git LFS.
#
# Every rebuild replaces ~78 MB of incompressible binaries (an AppImage, a
# Windows zip, a Linux tarball). Stored as ordinary blobs they accumulate in
# the pack forever and cannot be pruned without rewriting history, so a
# handful of refreshes is enough to make a clone painful. As LFS objects the
# working tree carries pointers instead, and old versions can be dropped from
# the LFS store when they stop mattering.
#
# This only stops the growth from here on. Deliverables committed before this
# rule are still plain blobs in the existing history.
07_Delivery/*.AppImage filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
07_Delivery/*.deb filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
07_Delivery/*.zip filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
07_Delivery/*.tar.gz filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

